# Cardinal System — Caddy configuration (host-level alternative)
#
# If you are NOT using the containerized Caddy inside the cardinal pod,
# you can run Caddy directly on the host and proxy to the pod's exposed port.
#
# With the pod running, the backend is available at 127.0.0.1:8080 (mapped
# from the pod's port 80 via cardinal-caddy).

# Production (VPS): uncomment once the domain is ready
# cardinal.example.com {
#     reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
# }

# Local: proxies to the cardinal pod
:8080 {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080
}

# ── Podman pod architecture ──────────────────────────────────
# The cardinal pod contains three containers sharing a network:
#   cardinal-caddy    (port 80 inside pod → host 8080)
#   cardinal-frontend (nginx, port 8000, serves SPA + proxies /api and /ws)
#   cardinal-backend  (Bun, port 8787, API + WebSocket server)
#
# Caddy → frontend:8000 → backend:8787
#
# The containerized Caddyfile lives at deploy/Caddyfile and gets
# mounted into the cardinal-caddy container at /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.
